<phyphox version="1.20" locale="en">
    <title>CO₂ Calibration</title>
    <category>phyphox:mini</category>
    <color>ADEBB3</color>
    <description>Forced recalibration of the STCC4 CO₂ sensor of a phyphox:mini. Take the phyphox:mini into fresh air, press start and watch the reading settle. Then press "Start calibration": the sensor measures for 30 s and sets itself to the reference value. The status shows whether the calibration is still running or finished. Afterwards "Resume measurement" shows the calibrated reading.

A reading stuck at exactly 380 ppm is the lower limit of the sensor output. The sensor then reads too low and needs this calibration.

The calibration permanently changes the sensor's calibration.</description>
    <translations>
        <translation locale="de">
            <title>CO₂-Kalibrierung</title>
            <category>phyphox:mini</category>
            <description>Kalibrierung (Forced Recalibration) des CO₂-Sensors STCC4 eines phyphox:mini. Bringe den phyphox:mini an die frische Luft, drücke Start und warte, bis sich der Messwert beruhigt hat. Dann „Kalibrierung starten“ drücken: Der Sensor misst 30 s lang und stellt sich auf den Referenzwert ein. Die Statusanzeige zeigt, ob die Kalibrierung noch läuft oder fertig ist. Danach zeigt „Messung fortsetzen“ den kalibrierten Messwert.

Ein Messwert, der genau bei 380 ppm stehen bleibt, ist die Untergrenze der Sensorausgabe. Der Sensor misst dann zu niedrig und braucht diese Kalibrierung.

Die Kalibrierung verändert die Kalibrierung des Sensors dauerhaft.</description>
            <string original="Calibration">Kalibrierung</string>
            <string original="1. Put the phyphox:mini in fresh air (outdoors or at a wide open window) and press start. 2. Wait until the CO₂ reading has settled - one to two minutes. 3. Press &quot;Start calibration&quot; and leave the phyphox:mini in the fresh air until the status says finished.">1. Den phyphox:mini an die frische Luft bringen (draußen oder am weit geöffneten Fenster) und Start drücken. 2. Warten, bis sich der CO₂-Wert beruhigt hat – ein bis zwei Minuten. 3. „Kalibrierung starten“ drücken und den phyphox:mini an der frischen Luft lassen, bis der Status „fertig“ anzeigt.</string>
            <string original="CO₂ (latest reading)">CO₂ (letzter Messwert)</string>
            <string original="Status">Status</string>
            <string original="measuring - ready to calibrate">Messung läuft – bereit zur Kalibrierung</string>
            <string original="calibration running - keep in fresh air">Kalibrierung läuft – an der frischen Luft lassen</string>
            <string original="calibration finished">Kalibrierung abgeschlossen</string>
            <string original="Time remaining">Restzeit</string>
            <string original="Reference value (fresh air)">Referenzwert (Frischluft)</string>
            <string original="Start calibration">Kalibrierung starten</string>
            <string original="Resume measurement">Messung fortsetzen</string>
            <string original="While the calibration runs and after it has finished, the phyphox:mini sends no new readings. Press &quot;Resume measurement&quot; afterwards: in fresh air the reading should now be close to the reference value.">Während der Kalibrierung und danach sendet der phyphox:mini keine neuen Messwerte. Anschließend „Messung fortsetzen“ drücken: An der frischen Luft sollte der Wert jetzt nahe am Referenzwert liegen.</string>
            <string original="Time (s)">Zeit (s)</string>
        </translation>
    </translations>

    <!--
        The STCC4 config characteristic cddf100c takes two bytes:
          byte 0 = 0x01 measure, 0x02 forced recalibration
          byte 1 = measure: interval in 100 ms steps
                   calibration: reference concentration in 10 ppm steps
        On connect the experiment only starts measuring (010A, one reading per
        second). The calibration is sent by the button, not on connect: the old
        version calibrated right away on connecting, often before the sensor
        had settled in fresh air.

        What the firmware does on 0x02: stop the measurement (1.2 s), measure
        continuously for 30 s, stop again (1.2 s), apply the recalibration.
        It does not report back when it is done, so the status here is a
        countdown from the moment the button was pressed. CAL_S = 35 s leaves
        a few seconds of margin on top of the ~32.5 s the firmware needs.
        After the recalibration the sensor stays idle and the firmware sends
        nothing (older firmware sent 0 ppm instead) until "Resume measurement"
        writes 010A again.
    -->
    <data-containers>
        <container size="0">co2_time_raw</container>
        <container size="0">co2_time</container>
        <container size="1">co2_timeOffset</container>
        <container size="0">co2</container>

        <!-- what the buttons send, both bytes go out together on trigger "send" -->
        <container size="1" init="1">cmd</container>
        <container size="1" init="10">arg</container>

        <container size="1" init="420">ref_ppm</container>
        <container size="1" init="42">ref_byte</container>

        <container size="1" init="0">t_now</container>
        <container size="1" init="0">cal_t0</container>
        <container size="1" init="0">cal_started</container>
        <container size="1" init="0">phase</container>
        <container size="1" init="0">remaining</container>
    </data-containers>

    <input>
        <bluetooth id="phyphox:mini" name="phyphox:mini" mode="notification" mtu="247" subscribeOnStart="true">
            <config char="cddf100c-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" conversion="hexadecimal">010A</config>
            <output char="cddf100b-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="0" conversion="float32LittleEndian">co2</output>
            <output char="cddf100b-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" offset="4" conversion="float32LittleEndian">co2_time_raw</output>
        </bluetooth>
    </input>

    <output>
        <bluetooth id="phyphox:mini">
            <input keep="true" char="cddf100c-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="0" triggerId="send">cmd</input>
            <input keep="true" char="cddf100c-30f7-4671-8b43-5e40ba53514a" length="1" conversion="singleByte" offset="1" triggerId="send">arg</input>
        </bluetooth>
    </output>

    <views>
        <view label="Calibration">
            <info label="1. Put the phyphox:mini in fresh air (outdoors or at a wide open window) and press start. 2. Wait until the CO₂ reading has settled - one to two minutes. 3. Press &quot;Start calibration&quot; and leave the phyphox:mini in the fresh air until the status says finished."/>
            <separator height="1"/>
            <value label="CO₂ (latest reading)" unit="ppm" size="2" precision="0">
                <input>co2</input>
            </value>
            <separator height="1"/>
            <value label="Status" size="1.2">
                <input>phase</input>
                <map max="0.5">measuring - ready to calibrate</map>
                <map min="0.5" max="1.5">calibration running - keep in fresh air</map>
                <map min="1.5">calibration finished</map>
            </value>
            <value label="Time remaining" unit="s" size="1.2" precision="0">
                <input>remaining</input>
                <map max="0">-</map>
            </value>
            <separator height="1"/>
            <edit label="Reference value (fresh air)" unit="ppm" default="420" min="380" max="2550" signed="false" decimal="false">
                <output>ref_ppm</output>
            </edit>
            <button label="Start calibration">
                <input type="value">2</input>
                <output>cmd</output>
                <input>ref_byte</input>
                <output>arg</output>
                <input>t_now</input>
                <output>cal_t0</output>
                <input type="value">1</input>
                <output>cal_started</output>
                <trigger>send</trigger>
            </button>
            <button label="Resume measurement">
                <input type="value">1</input>
                <output>cmd</output>
                <input type="value">10</input>
                <output>arg</output>
                <input type="value">0</input>
                <output>cal_started</output>
                <trigger>send</trigger>
            </button>
            <info label="While the calibration runs and after it has finished, the phyphox:mini sends no new readings. Press &quot;Resume measurement&quot; afterwards: in fresh air the reading should now be close to the reference value."/>
        </view>
    </views>

    <analysis sleep="0.2">
        <!-- wall clock, keeps running through a pause like the sensor does -->
        <timer linearTime="true">
            <output as="out">t_now</output>
        </timer>

        <!-- the firmware takes the reference in 10 ppm steps -->
        <formula formula="round([1]/10)">
            <input as="in" clear="false">ref_ppm</input>
            <output as="out">ref_byte</output>
        </formula>

        <!-- 0 = measuring, 1 = calibration running, 2 = finished; CAL_S = 35 s -->
        <formula formula="[3]*(1+heaviside([1]-[2]-35))">
            <input as="in" clear="false">t_now</input>
            <input as="in" clear="false">cal_t0</input>
            <input as="in" clear="false">cal_started</input>
            <output as="out">phase</output>
        </formula>
        <formula formula="[3]*max(0,35-([1]-[2]))">
            <input as="in" clear="false">t_now</input>
            <input as="in" clear="false">cal_t0</input>
            <input as="in" clear="false">cal_started</input>
            <output as="out">remaining</output>
        </formula>

        <first>
            <input as="value" clear="false">co2_time_raw</input>
            <output as="first">co2_timeOffset</output>
        </first>
        <subtract>
            <input as="minuend" clear="false">co2_time_raw</input>
            <input as="subtrahend" clear="false">co2_timeOffset</input>
            <output as="difference">co2_time</output>
        </subtract>
    </analysis>

    <export>
        <set name="CO₂">
            <data name="Time (s)">co2_time</data>
            <data name="CO₂ (ppm)">co2</data>
        </set>
    </export>
</phyphox>
